course: dictionary
lesson: 8709
title: One word, three meanings: names and peoples
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A word with a capital letter, like Seneca, is often a name for a particular person, people or place. Look at the words around it to see which one it is. Ask yourself: is it a person, a group of people, or a place?
explain: «Five, later six, nations, including the Mohawk and Seneca, formed the Haudenosaunee Confederacy.» Here Seneca names one of the nations, a people. The words «nations» and «formed» are the clues, because a nation is a group, not one person.
explain: «Seneca Falls» has a second word after it, and that tells you it is a town. Seneca the Younger, in a philosophy lesson, is a person. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check that it fits.
fact: Seneca is a name with a capital letter, so it names a particular person, people or place.
fact: Seneca the Roman was a thinker and writer, about 4 BC to AD 65, who wrote letters about living wisely and calmly.
fact: Seneca taught the emperor Nero, and his sayings are still quoted, such as «We suffer more often in imagination than in reality.»
fact: The Seneca are a Native American (First Nations) people, part of the Haudenosaunee Confederacy in New York State and Ontario.
fact: Seneca Falls is a town in New York, where a famous women's rights meeting took place in 1848.
exercise: «Five, later six, nations, including the Mohawk and Seneca, formed the Haudenosaunee Confederacy.» Here Seneca names what? | A town with a famous meeting | *A people, one of the nations | A kind of waterfall | A Roman thinker who wrote letters
exercise: Seneca was a Roman thinker who wrote letters about living calmly. Who did he teach? | *The emperor Nero | Julius Caesar | Sir Isaac Newton | Queen Victoria
exercise: In which US state is the town of «Seneca Falls»? | Texas | *New York | Ohio | Florida
test: In «Seneca Falls», what does the capital letter tell you? | It is a number | *It is the name of a place | It is a colour | It is an action word
test: In «The Seneca are one of the Six Nations», what does the Seneca mean? | A Roman writer | *A people, like the Mohawk | A town in New York | A kind of falls
exam: «Seneca wrote letters about living wisely and calmly; he was a Stoic philosopher.» Here Seneca names | a place in Ontario | a people of the Confederacy | a town where a meeting took place | *a person, a Roman thinker
